<title>USA: Nemdaco spinning off Hydroponix.</title>
<headline>Nemdaco spinning off Hydroponix.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nemdaco Inc said Monday it declared a stock dividend of one share of Hydroponix Inc common stock for each four shares of Nemdaco Inc common stock owned on the record date of February 28, 1997.</p>
<p>Hydroponix (formerly Nemdaco Attache Communications) was formed to grow and market high quality specialty crops, initially tomatoes, in controlled environment greenhouses.</p>
<p>Nemdaco said the facilities will be built in Puerto Rico. Each acre will contain about 11,000 tomato plants, capable of producing over 396,000 pounds, Nemdaco said. Annual per acre revenues are expected to be $495,000.</p>
</text>
